  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "The text 'I am against gun, violence and discrimination' is mapped onto the smiling Black man in the foreground.",
  "description": "The text explicitly states 'I am against...', which directly projects the speaker's identity (the person who is against these issues) onto the visual entity — the Black man in the foreground. His joyful expression, rainbow lanyard, and presence at a Pride event visually represent his identity as an ally and advocate for the causes mentioned in the text. The mapping is established by the textual 'I' being attributed to the visual subject, making him the embodiment of the message. This is a classic analogical mapping where the visual subject is identified as the speaker of the text.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
